Package: staleness
Type: Package
Title: Apply and Calibrate Published Signals for Updating Meta-Analyses
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Javier", "Núñez", email = "jnverbel@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-9770-4986"))
Description: Implements the five published statistical methods for detecting whether a
    systematic review or meta-analysis has gone out of date, and provides a
    backtesting engine to calibrate those methods against historical evidence.
    Methods implemented follow Shojania and colleagues (2007) <doi:10.7326/0003-4819-147-4-200708210-00179>
    and the comparative evaluation of updating signals in the evidence synthesis
    literature. The published methods are applied and also evaluated critically:
    where a source's own statistic is invalid, a calibrated substitute is used
    in its place, the original quantity is still reported as a diagnostic, and
    the detector is named for the substitution rather than for the method it
    departs from - as in 'sufficiency_changepoint()', whose stability half
    replaces a regression slope that flagged 209 of 300 samples containing no
    change at all. Every departure is measured and documented in the
    corresponding help page and in the 'methods' vignette, so that results are
    not read as a literal reproduction. The backtesting targets are operational
    definitions of the pooled estimate having moved, not recorded decisions by
    review teams, so a reported sensitivity means agreement with a stated
    criterion rather than correctness; that bound is documented rather than
    left to be inferred. The package performs no literature searching and no
    screening.
